From e9c4fe79a11b49618ffd5c7e6cd8c78040e597cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:19:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/31] fix(token-capture): ignore think-wrapped reasoning in
 assistant fingerprints

With uses_reasoning_parser: true the vLLM model server folds the parsed
reasoning into the reply as "<think>REASONING</think>" + content
(_wrap_reasoning_in_think_tags, app.py) before _finalize_external_capture
records the call. The ledger row's continuation fingerprint therefore
covered the think block. A harness that echoes the reply without its
reasoning (LiteLLM splits the leading block back out; Terminus-2 with
interleaved_thinking: false sends only the content; a Responses harness
gets the reasoning as a standalone item) produced a fingerprint that
matched no row: no_match -> unresolved_parent, rollout rejected. The
terminal content witness compared against the same think-wrapped
fingerprints and failed the same way.

Fix: assistant_fingerprint strips the leading run of <think>...</think>
blocks from the first text part of every model-authored item, on both
the recorded and the incoming side. Reasoning in the content is thereby
excluded like standalone reasoning items already were, and a call
resolves whether the harness echoes the think block or not. Only a
leading run is stripped: that is the only place the server puts
reasoning, think tags later in visible text stay hashed, and stripping
the whole run (not one block) is idempotent, so a reply whose visible
text itself opens with a block still matches LiteLLM's one-block split.
A reasoning-only reply strips to no text and hashes the empty-turn
marker, like "" or None; a tool call with reasoning and no content
hashes like the bare tool call. User and tool content is not touched.

conversation_digest is unchanged: it only ever hashes request items as
the harness sent them (stamp_continuation, FileLineageStore._record and
_resolve_row digest request_items, never the served reply), so a harness
that echoes consistently passes it with or without reasoning.

FINGERPRINT_VERSION goes to 3: fingerprints of histories with a
think-wrapped assistant turn change, so rows stamped by an older server
are ignored. No existing golden vector changes; new vectors pin a
think-wrapped reply (equal to the plain vector) and a reasoning-only
reply (equal to an empty turn).

Evidence (job 5302914, Terminus-2, interleaved_thinking false, Apertus 2
SFT model thinking on turn 0): 173/192 rollouts rejected with
unresolved_parent. Replaying 188 rollouts from the Terminus-2 episode
prompts/replies reproduces every committed v2 row exactly (fingerprint,
context_len, context_digest), and the v2 replay predicts the observed
first unresolved call in 188/188. With the v3 fingerprint every call of
all 188 rollouts (751 calls, 180 with reasoning; 169 rejected in
production) resolves to the call right before it, both with and without
the think block echoed. 4 rollouts could not be reconstructed.

Tests: test_token_capture_think_reasoning.py (33 cases, 23 fail without
the fix), golden vectors.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
